## Using JPA + Hibernate – A Practical How‑to Guide

> **Short answer** – *Hibernate is a JPA implementation. To “use JPA with Hibernate” you:*
> 1. Add the JPA API and the Hibernate provider to your project.  
> 2. Declare a persistence unit (XML or annotations).  
> 3. Map your Java classes to tables with JPA annotations.  
> 4. Obtain an `EntityManager` (or a Spring‑managed `JpaRepository`) and run CRUD / JPQL / Criteria queries inside transactions.

Below is a step‑by‑step walkthrough that covers:

| Section | What you’ll learn |
|---------|--------------------|
| 1 | Project setup (Maven/Gradle) |
| 2 | JPA persistence configuration |
| 3 | Entity mapping basics |
| 4 | CRUD with `EntityManager` |
| 5 | JPQL & Criteria API |
| 6 | Advanced features (lazy, cascade, caching) |
| 7 | Spring Boot + Spring Data JPA integration |
| 8 | Debugging & performance tips |

---

## 1. Project Setup

### Maven

```xml
<dependencies>
    <!-- JPA API -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>jakarta.persistence</groupId>
        <artifactId>jakarta.persistence-api</artifactId>
        <version>3.1.0</version>   <!-- JPA 3.x -->
    </dependency>

    <!-- Hibernate Core (JPA implementation) -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.hibernate.orm</groupId>
        <artifactId>hibernate-core</artifactId>
        <version>6.2.5.Final</version>
    </dependency>

    <!-- (Optional) Hibernate EntityManager – bundled in Hibernate‑Core 6.x -->
    <!-- (Optional) HikariCP or any JDBC connection pool -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>com.zaxxer</groupId>
        <artifactId>HikariCP</artifactId>
        <version>5.0.1</version>
    </dependency>

    <!-- Database driver -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.postgresql</groupId>
        <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
        <version>42.7.3</version>
    </dependency>

    <!-- For JUnit tests -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
        <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
        <version>5.11.0</version>
        <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
</dependencies>
```

### Gradle (Kotlin DSL)

```kotlin
dependencies {
    implementation("jakarta.persistence:jakarta.persistence-api:3.1.0")
    implementation("org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-core:6.2.5.Final")
    implementation("com.zaxxer:HikariCP:5.0.1")
    runtimeOnly("org.postgresql:postgresql:42.7.3")
    testImplementation("org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter:5.11.0")
}
```

