## 2. Persistence Configuration

### Option A – `persistence.xml`

```xml
<!-- src/main/resources/META-INF/persistence.xml -->
<persistence xmlns="https://jakarta.ee/xml/ns/persistence"
             xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
             xsi:schemaLocation="https://jakarta.ee/xml/ns/persistence
                                 https://jakarta.ee/xml/ns/persistence/persistence_3_0.xsd"
             version="3.0">

    <persistence-unit name="demoPU" transaction-type="RESOURCE_LOCAL">
        <!-- Entities are auto‑scanned in the same package or subpackages -->
        <class>com.example.demo.model.User</class>
        <class>com.example.demo.model.Role</class>

        <!-- Hibernate provider -->
        <provider>org.hibernate.jpa.HibernatePersistenceProvider</provider>

        <!-- JDBC connection -->
        <properties>
            <property name="jakarta.persistence.jdbc.driver" value="org.postgresql.Driver"/>
            <property name="jakarta.persistence.jdbc.url"     value="jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/demo"/>
            <property name="jakarta.persistence.jdbc.user"   value="demo"/>
            <property name="jakarta.persistence.jdbc.password" value="demo"/>

            <!-- Hibernate dialect -->
            <property name="hibernate.dialect" value="org.hibernate.dialect.PostgreSQLDialect"/>

            <!-- Show SQL in console -->
            <property name="hibernate.show_sql" value="true"/>
            <property name="hibernate.format_sql" value="true"/>

            <!-- Schema generation -->
            <property name="hibernate.hbm2ddl.auto" value="update"/> <!-- create, update, validate, none -->
        </properties>
    </persistence-unit>
</persistence>
```

### Option B – Java‑based configuration (pure JPA, no XML)

```java
// src/main/java/com/example/demo/config/EntityManagerFactoryProducer.java
@ApplicationScoped
public class EntityManagerFactoryProducer {

    @Produces
    @Singleton
    public EntityManagerFactory produce() {
        Map<String, Object> props = new HashMap<>();
        props.put("jakarta.persistence.jdbc.driver", "org.postgresql.Driver");
        props.put("jakarta.persistence.jdbc.url", "jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/demo");
        props.put("jakarta.persistence.jdbc.user", "demo");
        props.put("jakarta.persistence.jdbc.password", "demo");
        props.put("hibernate.dialect", "org.hibernate.dialect.PostgreSQLDialect");
        props.put("hibernate.show_sql", true);
        props.put("hibernate.format_sql", true);
        props.put("hibernate.hbm2ddl.auto", "update");
        return Persistence.createEntityManagerFactory("demoPU", props);
    }
}
```

> **Tip** – In a **Spring Boot** app you only need the `spring-boot-starter-data-jpa` dependency and `application.yml`. Spring auto‑configures the `EntityManagerFactory`.

