## 3. Mapping Entities

### Basic entity

```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "users")
@Getter @Setter @NoArgsConstructor
public class User {

    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY) // auto‑increment
    private Long id;

    @Column(nullable = false, unique = true)
    private String username;

    @Column(nullable = false)
    private String password;

    // One-to-many: a user has many roles
    @OneToMany(mappedBy = "user", cascade = CascadeType.ALL, orphanRemoval = true, fetch = FetchType.LAZY)
    private List<Role> roles = new ArrayList<>();

    // Convenience
    public void addRole(Role role) {
        roles.add(role);
        role.setUser(this);
    }
}
```

### Related entity

```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "roles")
@Getter @Setter @NoArgsConstructor
public class Role {

    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    @Column(nullable = false)
    private String name;

    @ManyToOne(fetch = FetchType.LAZY)
    @JoinColumn(name = "user_id", nullable = false)
    private User user;
}
```

> **Common annotations**  
> `@Entity`, `@Table` – marks the class and optionally specifies the table name.  
> `@Id`, `@GeneratedValue` – primary key generation strategy.  
> `@Column` – column constraints.  
> `@OneToMany`, `@ManyToOne`, `@OneToOne`, `@ManyToMany` – relationships.  
> `@Transient` – ignore field.  
> `@Embedded`, `@Embeddable` – value objects.  
> `@MappedSuperclass` – reuse common mapping.

