## 4. CRUD with `EntityManager`

```java
@Stateless // or @Repository / @Component (Spring)
public class UserDao {

    @PersistenceContext(unitName = "demoPU") // CDI or Spring injects EM
    private EntityManager em;

    public User find(Long id) {
        return em.find(User.class, id);
    }

    public User create(User user) {
        em.persist(user);
        return user; // after persist, id is generated
    }

    public User update(User user) {
        return em.merge(user);
    }

    public void delete(User user) {
        if (!em.contains(user)) {
            user = em.merge(user); // attach to context
        }
        em.remove(user);
    }

    // Query example
    public List<User> findAll() {
        TypedQuery<User> q = em.createQuery("SELECT u FROM User u", User.class);
        return q.getResultList();
    }
}
```

### Transaction management

* **Java SE / Jakarta EE** – manually begin/commit/rollback using `EntityTransaction`.
  ```java
  EntityManager em = emf.createEntityManager();
  EntityTransaction tx = em.getTransaction();
  try {
      tx.begin();
      // DAO calls
      tx.commit();
  } catch (Exception e) {
      if (tx.isActive()) tx.rollback();
      throw e;
  } finally {
      em.close();
  }
  ```

* **Jakarta EE** – container‑managed transactions (`@Transactional` or EJB).  
* **Spring** – `@Transactional` on service layer.

