## 7. Spring Boot + Spring Data JPA

```bash
# Add dependency
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-jpa</artifactId>
</dependency>
```

**application.yml**

```yaml
spring:
  datasource:
    url: jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/demo
    username: demo
    password: demo
  jpa:
    hibernate:
      ddl-auto: update
    show-sql: true
    properties:
      hibernate:
        format_sql: true
```

**Repository**

```java
public interface UserRepository extends JpaRepository<User, Long> {
    Optional<User> findByUsername(String username);
}
```

**Service**

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class UserService {

    private final UserRepository repo;

    @Transactional
    public User register(String user, String pass) {
        User u = new User();
        u.setUsername(user);
        u.setPassword(pass);
        return repo.save(u);
    }
}
```

Spring manages the `EntityManagerFactory`, transactions (`@Transactional`), and offers many conveniences (query derivation, specifications, pagination).

